      "severity": "major",
      "title": "Feedback FB-001 (behaviour): e2e/test_e2e_stack.py calls no pytest.skip",
      "detail": "Remove the two profile guards: the pytest.skip in _require_fake_profile (drop the helper and its six calls) and the pytest.skip in the injected_fault fixture. L4 integrity rejects any skip call or marker that a harness commit adds (F-5758ac1b, rounds 1 and 2), so the spec sentence \"call pytest.skip when it is not fake\" cannot be met by any harness commit. Profile selection belongs to markers (e2e/pyproject.toml has `stack` with addopts -m \"not stack\"), and the stack-profile run is out of this unit scope (proposal.md). Keep the e2e_profile parameters, test names, l4 markers and every assertion as they are. The red gate runs only Node tests, so the red test is a Node test that reads the file text, for example under test/arch/.",
      "source": "feedback",
      "criterion": null,
      "log": null,
      "spec_gap": false,
